{% comment %}
  Shared "appointment card" summary — doctor photo, "YOUR CONSULTATION"
  eyebrow, name, and a mode + price row. Slot Picker (node 438:7388) and
  Patient Details (node 438:7643) both use this exact composition per
  their Figma specs, so it's extracted here instead of duplicating the
  markup per step (same reasoning as kal-booking-flow-step-header.liquid).

  Mode text (data-kal-summary-mode) is kept in sync with the In-Clinic/
  Video Consult toggle on Doctor Select by kal-booking-flow.js's setMode —
  no extra wiring needed here, every instance of this snippet just picks
  up the same live text.

  Accepts:
  - photo_url: {String} doctor photo URL — no longer used, kept as a
    param so existing render calls don't need updating; the photo is a
    plain placeholder box for now (see .kal-doctor-photo-placeholder in
    the CSS), removed everywhere in this flow per explicit instruction
  - name: {String} e.g. "Dr. Neethu Jayachandran"
  - price: {String} pre-formatted, e.g. "&#8377;500"

  Usage:
  {% render 'kal-booking-flow-appointment-card', photo_url: doctor_photo_url, name: 'Dr. Neethu Jayachandran', price: '&#8377;500' %}
{% endcomment %}

<div class="kal-appointment-card">
  <span class="kal-appointment-card__photo" data-kal-doctor-photo-display>
    <span class="kal-doctor-photo-placeholder"></span>
  </span>
  <span class="kal-appointment-card__body">
    <span class="kal-appointment-card__eyebrow">Your Consultation</span>
    <span class="kal-appointment-card__name" data-kal-doctor-name-display>{{ name }}</span>
    <span class="kal-appointment-card__meta">
      <span data-kal-summary-mode>In-Clinic</span>
      <span class="kal-appointment-card__divider" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span data-kal-doctor-price-display>{{ price }}</span>
    </span>
  </span>
</div>
